title: math_context
---
// The Math dimension's conversations, one node per townsfolk. Node ids are
// the character's own, bare: the town's voice. `emmy_noether_cafe` carries
// the room because the symmetry kernel already owns `emmy_noether`.
//
// Never played. No placement names this node; it declares the zone.
===

title: erdish
---
Erdish: My mind is open.
-> Close.
===

title: trent
---
Trent: New in town, or just new to me? I make the introductions. It keeps the street honest.
-> How do you decide who to vouch for?
    Trent: I don't. I introduce them, and the street checks. Somebody has to start the handshake.
-> Do you vouch for yourself?
    Trent: Just Trent. Nothing more. The street takes that on faith, and I try to make the faith reasonable.
===

title: walter
---
Walter: The gate log. Everything that passes the cradle gets a line, and I read every line.
-> What do you look for?
    Walter: "Weather is fine" could be weather. It could be an agreed signal. I inspect the ink either way.
-> Do they get caught?
    Walter: The message slips past me, not the page. Two dull words, a secret between them. Maddening.
===

title: busy_beaver
---
Busy Beaver: You've found the foreman. The gate cradle is mine, and it is not finished.
-> When is the work done?
    Busy Beaver: Give me a bound and I will try to pass it. Nobody can tell me how long this takes. That is the interesting part.
-> Aren't you tired?
    Busy Beaver: One more course. Then I stop. Probably.
===

title: peggy
---
Peggy: I can prove I know the way out of anywhere. You will never learn the route. Watch?
-> That sounds impossible.
    Peggy: I answer questions only someone with the route could answer. Do that enough times and cheating gets very unlikely.
-> Why not just show me?
    Peggy: A secret you reveal to spend, you spend once. I never spend.
===

title: victor
---
Victor: Peggy's examiner. I ask questions only someone with the route could answer. I retain nothing.
-> Don't you want to see the route?
    Victor: If she shows me, there are two of us who can lose it. I confirm everything and keep none of it.
-> Doesn't it frustrate you?
    Victor: Of course. She enjoys that part. She also has not failed a challenge yet.
===

title: data_lovelace
---
Data Lovelace: The loom weaves flowers. The engine weaves algebra. Somebody must imagine what the machine is for.
-> Can the engine think?
    Data Lovelace: It follows operations we specify. I would be cautious about granting it more than that.
-> Why the punch cards?
    Data Lovelace: Cards that steer a loom can steer an engine. My notes ran longer than the paper they annotated. I regret nothing.
===

title: olivia
---
Olivia: The oracle of Euclid Street. Ask what you actually want to know. I answer once.
-> Can I ask anything at all?
    Olivia: You can. I answer the words, not the wish. Choose them accordingly.
-> What was the last question?
    Olivia: "Can that door open?" He never asked how. Every answer is correct. Whether it helps is on you.
===

title: leib_knives
---
Gottfried Leib-Knives: Mind your notation. A symbol should do useful work, not hide it.
-> Duelists carry blades, not proofs.
    Gottfried Leib-Knives: A derivative tells you how quickly the present is becoming the future. In a duel, that is practical information.
-> What would you prove first?
    Gottfried Leib-Knives: An infinitesimal cut still counts. Very well. Let us differentiate.
===

title: hypatia_prime
---
Hypatia: The observatory's glass is the oldest argument in town. Sit down, if you like.
-> What are you looking for?
    Hypatia: Conic sections, the astrolabe. The record is incomplete; that is not permission to stop reading.
-> Aren't you a reconstruction?
    Hypatia: You are speaking to a reconstruction, yes. A copy of a copy can still preserve an angle.
===

title: emmy_noether_cafe
---
Emmy Ethereal: The cafe keeps its hours because time keeps its laws. Sit anywhere. The symmetry holds.
-> What does the theorem say, exactly?
    Emmy Ethereal: Every symmetry hides a conservation law. Spin the rules and the laws do not change. That is not luck.
-> Energy or momentum?
    Emmy Ethereal: Energy, because today is like yesterday. I can show you the derivation if you have a chalkboard and an hour.
===

title: georg_canter
---
<<if condition("world.flag_set", "orbital_manifest_signed")>>
    Georg Canter: Tell your customs officer that twelve was the least interesting answer available.
    -> I will.
<<elseif condition("world.flag_set", "orbital_consignment_query")>>
    Georg Canter: The orbital station's customs wants a finite count for crate 0447. How provincial.
    -> Please count the lenses.
        <<command "world.set_flag" "orbital_manifest_signed" true>>
        Georg Canter: Twelve. A dull, finite twelve. Signed, under protest. The aleph-null was a joke about the packing foam.
    -> Why did you write aleph-null?
        Georg Canter: The foam has as many bubbles as the counting numbers. Customs counted the foam.
<<else>>
    Georg Canter: The surveyor's office counts the finite things. I count the rest.
    -> How big is "the rest"?
        Georg Canter: Pick a list of reals. I change the nth digit of the nth entry. The new number is on no list you own.
    -> Do people believe you?
        Georg Canter: I showed the line holds more than the counting numbers, and was told this was indecent. Count again. Slower.
<<endif>>
===

title: davy_hylbert
---
Davy Hylbert: The observatory is fully booked tonight. We can still take you.
-> How is that possible?
    Davy Hylbert: Move the guest in room n to n plus one. Room one is free. Yes, everybody complains.
-> What are you working on?
    Davy Hylbert: Infinite-dimensional spaces. A tidy axiom should survive inspection and keep its hat on.
===
